source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: The `*` run of the same length reaches the same fabricated empty level, and jiro answers it with the same escaped line and the same two warnings.
-- input.jira --
* a
*** b
-- rendered.html --
<ul>
	<li>a
	<ul>
		<li>
		<ul>
			<li>b</li>
		</ul>
		</li>
	</ul>
	</li>
</ul>
-- want.md --
- a

\*\*\* b
-- warnings.json --
[
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "list",
    "Reason": "list nesting skips an authored parent level"
  },
  {
    "Line": 2,
    "Column": 1,
    "Construct": "list",
    "Reason": "list item has no parent at its authored nesting level"
  }
]
